From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] mfd: mtk-spmi-pmic: add MediaTek MT6685

The MT6685 holds the RTC and the clock buffer of the MT6897 boards. It has
no interrupt groups like the other PMICs here, so there is no variant, and
its sub-devices are all it needs from this driver.

Without a variant, probing only populates the children. It makes no
regmap, as that would give debugfs a way to read the whole chip, including
the RTC registers that clear when read. It doesn't read the chip ID either:
the register holding it for the other PMICs here isn't in what is known of
this one, and the MediaTek driver for this chip doesn't read anything
either. So nothing on the bus happens because of this driver.

Without children it binds and does nothing, which is what the connectivity
subsystem needs: that only looks up the device of this node and reads a
register through the SPMI bus.
---
 drivers/mfd/mtk-spmi-pmic.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mfd/mtk-spmi-pmic.c b/drivers/mfd/mtk-spmi-pmic.c
index 33b469b..5828fab 100644
--- a/drivers/mfd/mtk-spmi-pmic.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/mtk-spmi-pmic.c
@@ -454,6 +454,11 @@ static int mtk_spmi_pmic_probe(struct spmi_device *sdev)
 	unsigned int chip_id;
 	int ret;
 
+	/* Without interrupts, the sub-devices need nothing from here */
+	variant = device_get_match_data(dev);
+	if (!variant)
+		return devm_of_platform_populate(dev);
+
 	regmap = devm_regmap_init_spmi_ext(sdev, &mtk_spmi_regmap_config);
 	if (IS_ERR(regmap))
 		return PTR_ERR(regmap);
@@ -465,8 +470,7 @@ static int mtk_spmi_pmic_probe(struct spmi_device *sdev)
 	 */
 	regmap_read(regmap, MTK_SPMI_PMIC_REG_CHIP_ID, &chip_id);
 
-	variant = device_get_match_data(dev);
-	if (variant && variant->num_groups) {
+	if (variant->num_groups) {
 		ret = mtk_spmi_pmic_irq_init(dev, regmap, variant);
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
@@ -479,6 +483,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id mtk_pmic_spmi_id_table[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "mediatek,mt6363", .data = &mt6363_variant },
 	{ .compatible = "mediatek,mt6368", .data = &mt6368_variant },
 	{ .compatible = "mediatek,mt6373", .data = &mt6373_variant },
+	{ .compatible = "mediatek,mt6685" },
 	{ /* sentinel */ }
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, mtk_pmic_spmi_id_table);
